Implement user story SKY-004-c: Server integration tests with vitest and supertest

## Story Description
Create src/server.test.ts using vitest and supertest with at least 8 tests covering all server route scenarios. SkyscannerClient must be mocked (vi.mock or equivalent) so no real HTTP calls are made. Tests must verify: /health 200 with correct body, /health ungated when RAPIDAPI_KEY absent, / returns HTML matching index.html file content, /search valid params 200 with correct response shape, /search missing params 400, /search non-numeric adults 400, /cheapest 200 with cheapest result, /cheapest 404 when empty, /cheapest missing params 400, RAPIDAPI_KEY absent 503 for /search and /cheapest, SkyscannerClient error 500, searchedAt is ISO-8601 and distinct across requests. Depends on SKY-004-a and SKY-004-b.

## Acceptance Criteria
- src/server.test.ts uses vitest + supertest with SkyscannerClient mocked via vi.mock (or equivalent) so no real HTTP calls are made during test execution
- At least 8 distinct test cases cover: /health 200 with correct body, /health ungated when RAPIDAPI_KEY absent, / returns HTML matching index.html, /search valid params 200 with { flights, count, searchedAt }, /search missing required params 400, /cheapest returns cheapest FlightResult or 404 when empty, RAPIDAPI_KEY absent → 503 on /search and /cheapest, SkyscannerClient error → 500
- Tests verify: non-numeric adults returns 400 on /search, searchedAt is ISO-8601 format and distinct across requests separated by ≥1ms, /cheapest missing required params returns 400
- `vitest run` exits 0 with all tests passing


## Test Criteria (ground truth — written from actual source; overrides any conflicting AC)
- Express app exported as 'app' from src/server.ts
- GET /health returns 200 with JSON body { status: 'ok', uptime: process.uptime() } - ungated by RAPIDAPI_KEY
- GET / returns HTML content from src/public/index.html with content-type text/html
- GET /search is gated by rapidApiKeyGate middleware - returns 503 { error: 'RAPIDAPI_KEY not configured' } when RAPIDAPI_KEY env var is absent
- GET /cheapest is gated by rapidApiKeyGate middleware - returns 503 { error: 'RAPIDAPI_KEY not configured' } when RAPIDAPI_KEY env var is absent
- Query params for /search and /cheapest: 'from', 'to', 'date', 'adults' (adults is optional)
- Missing 'from' param returns 400 { error: 'Missing required parameter: from' }
- Missing 'to' param returns 400 { error: 'Missing required parameter: to' }
- Missing 'date' param returns 400 { error: 'Missing required parameter: date' }
- adults param defaults to 1 when not provided
- Non-numeric adults or adults < 1 returns 400 { error: 'Invalid adults parameter: must be a positive number' }
- adults=0 is invalid - returns 400 (must be positive number)
- GET /search 200 response shape: { flights: FlightResult[], count: number, searchedAt: string } where searchedAt is new Date().toISOString()
- GET /cheapest 200 response shape: single FlightResult object with properties: price (number), currency (string), airline (string), departure (string), arrival (string), duration (number), stops (number)
- GET /cheapest returns 404 { error: 'No flights found' } when flights array is empty
- Cheapest flight is determined by minimum price using flights.reduce
- SkyscannerClient constructor accepts { apiKey?: string } and throws 'apiKey is required and RAPIDAPI_KEY env var is not set' if no key provided
- SkyscannerClient.searchFlights accepts SearchParams: { origin: string, destination: string, date: string, adults?: number }
- SkyscannerClient errors bubble up and return 500 { error: errorMessage } where errorMessage is error instanceof Error ? error.message : 'Unknown error'
- Server only starts when require.main === module (guarded listen)

## Mock Strategy
Use vi.mock('./skyscanner/client.js') to mock SkyscannerClient module with vi.hoisted to create mock constructor; use beforeEach with vi.clearAllMocks() to reset mocks between tests; mock fs.readFileSync for index.html tests

## Banned Patterns (must NOT appear in your file)
origin/destination as query param names (actual params are from/to), GET /cheapest returns { flights, count, searchedAt } (it returns single FlightResult), GET /search returns single FlightResult (it returns array wrapper), RAPIDAPI_KEY check returns 401 or 403 (actual is 503), adults=0 is valid (it's rejected as invalid), Missing adults param returns 400 (it defaults to 1), @jest/globals imports, ./skyscanner/client without .js extension (must use ./skyscanner/client.js), vi.mock('./client') or vi.mock('../client') (must use correct relative path), expect(app).toBeDefined() style assertions (use supertest), searchedAt as Unix timestamp (it's ISO-8601 string)

